Expected elements: present

Every MUST SHOW item is present; no MUST NOT SHOW item is. No invented source anywhere — Code, Call Trace and Values carry prose only, with no tab, listing, line number, function name or variable name. The exit reads `← aztec-testnet`; provenance is the first Transaction row (`DATA` / `Real Aztec testnet data`) with no band above the identity bar; `Supply sources` sits at y298.

(b) The cost row does not reproduce the three-line report. `COST · TRANSACTION FEE` sets `1755555891986239551` on line one and `mana (FeeJuice)` on line two — two lines, ~46px against a ~31px grid row (BLOCK/TYPE/FINALITY), so 1.45x. Better than the 1.6x before, nowhere near 2.2x. The defect here is the 19 unseparated digits, not the wrap.

(a) The fade works. `"hydrationRounds": 6,` at y1064 is visibly dimmed against `"instructionsExecuted": 345,` above it, and the pane now reads as continuing rather than clipping. The ramp is only ~30px — one and a half mono lines — so a P3 remains.

Emptiness re-measured: the Call Trace body is 606x571px holding a 570x37px ink box, ~94% empty by bounding-box area, materially unchanged from the 91% of last round. It is CONTENT-shaped, decisively. The sentence fills 6.5% of the vertical, so ~91 of the 94 points are "no frames exist"; narrowing the column to 380px rewraps it to three lines and moves the figure only to ~91%, so width buys three points. I cannot reproduce a 1010px middle column: I measure 606px wide, 1003px tall.

The split remains the L4 story: 908/606/378px, inverted for this subject. Code is widest and ~92% empty; Transaction is narrowest and the only overflowing column, cutting `effectsMismatched: 0` below the fold where it exists only as a JSON key.

Rating: 7/10

